      <marc:subfield code="a">Cinema immortal Charles Chaplin brings his talents to both sides of the camera in this acclaimed Silent-Era classic, A woman of Paris, Chaplin&apos;s first drama ( agenre he visited again in Limelight) tells the tale of Marie St. Clair, who, believing she has been jilted by her artist fiance, goes off to Paris alone. Directing with keen-eyed finesse and appearing in only a bit role, Chaplin jabs at French high society while telling a tale of tragic love.</marc:subfield>
